# Bundled runtime (Python venv, Tesseract, etc.) — assembled at build time per BUILD.txt,
# never committed. Blanket-ignored so a stale vendor/ollama/ (removed 2026-07) can't reappear.
vendor/
dist/
node_modules/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
/processing.log
/processing_test.log

# Diagnostic logs (per-session JSONL + processing logs) — contain extracted
# document data; local diagnostic artefacts only, never committed.
Debug/
*.jsonl

# Licensing signing keys — private keys must NEVER be committed or bundled.
# Generated by licensing-backend/scripts/generate_keys.js; live only on the host.
# (`/*` not `/` so the SEC-02 deny backstop keys/.htaccess CAN be committed —
# a trailing-slash dir ignore would hide everything inside, exception included.)
licensing-backend/keys/*
!licensing-backend/keys/.htaccess

# Deployed backend copy (Build-IonosDeploy output) — a full on-host copy of the
# licensing backend that carries the SAME live private signing keys, admin password
# hash, and per-host config. Source of truth is licensing-backend/. Blanket-ignored
# so a stray `git add -A` can never stage the deployed secrets.
output/

# PHP per-directory config — host/deploy-specific. .user.ini carries the
# auto_prepend_file path to set-env.php and other per-host PHP settings (a
# REPLACE_ME template from Build-IonosDeploy, or the live host paths). Never committed.
licensing-backend/**/.user.ini

# Claude Code: machine-local settings + transient worktrees (the shared
# agents/ and skills/ ARE committed). settings.local.json holds per-host config.
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/worktrees/

# Runtime-learned templates: the app writes these to templatesDir (the repo
# templates/ dir in dev, userData when packaged) via _writeTemplateFile. They are
# per-install learned data, NOT shipped (not in build files/extraResources), so they
# must never be committed.
templates/*.json

# Private TLS key material must NEVER be committed (SECURITY_AUDIT.md F-07). The
# Samples/ tree holds throwaway demo certs (incl. ca.key / server.key / server.pfx,
# all of which carry a private key); ignore the whole tree, plus a belt-and-braces
# global rule for any stray private-key file anywhere in the repo.
Samples/
*.key
*.pfx
*.p12

# Generated synthetic test-harness corpus (rendered PDFs + page images + OCR JSON,
# multi-GB). Reproducible via `py -3.12 -m test_harness.run`; the HARNESS CODE
# (python_backend/test_harness/) is committed, but its OUTPUT is not.
python_backend/artifacts/

# Local extraction/fingerprinting research scratch (prototypes + a multi-hundred-MB
# OCR cache). The shipped harnesses live in stress_test/*.js; sandbox/ is throwaway.
sandbox/

# Generated measurement reports written by the stress_test harnesses.
stress_test/out/

# Parked website design variants + pricing model — kept out of the app repo but not
# deleted (recoverable). Move anything here back out if it's needed again.
_archive/

# Security audit + living backlog — contain concrete exploit detail for THIS product.
# Local working docs only; never committed/pushed so the repo history can't become an
# attacker roadmap. See SECURITY_BACKLOG.md (the tracker) + SECURITY_AUDIT_*.md (full evidence).
SECURITY_AUDIT_*.md
SECURITY_BACKLOG.md
